{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097066-launching-big-object","id":1097066,"title":"Launching big object","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-26T03:33:34-07:00","id":1097066,"title":"Launching big object","content":"Hi all, <br /> It's just happened, for the first time, in my cronichles, that a player of mine with high Vigor launched a car vs an enemy. <br /> The vigor rules for launchig such kind of objects are clear but, as he let me wonder, a car launched is a lot more hard to avoid. Meaning that, due to its size, is silly use the normal defense and still be able to act. So we thought that maybe such kind of attacks could be considered as no subject to normal defense apllication. Maybe to avoid this attacks should be necessary to spent the action for a dodge roll because the target has to litterally jump outside the car trajectory. <br /> <br /> What do you think about? Any other houserule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T04:59:26-07:00","id":1097077,"title":"","content":"I think arbitrarily ignoring someone's innate defense skill is silly. The Vigor using character has to spend their action that turn hefting and throwing the car and which entails an attack roll which they don't get bonuses to attack and the rules using improvised weapons doesn't negate a victims's defense. Why should throwing a car be a special snowflake case of ignoring defense when throwing dumpsters filled with garbage, a basket of rabid cats or an open vial containing a flesh dissolving acid requires overcoming defense? If mechanics lying on their back underneath a car can roll away unharmed when a jack holding the car up suddenly fails and the car crashes to the ground, yes it's entirely possible for someone to avoid a car being flung at them. If you're playing with trajectory arcs to throw the car the maximum distance it's a no brainer to run in the direction of the thrower and the car soars harmlessly overhead or just move a few feet to the left or right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T05:57:46-07:00","id":1097092,"title":"","content":"Well, bullets ignore defense... So I don't see why defense should be untouchable. <br /> My point is that defense is used vs punches and other things. You move your body with little shift in order to be harder to be hitted. <br /> While a car is a too big things to be avoided with just a shift of your chest or a step aside. <br /> Thats all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T06:51:17-07:00","id":1097107,"title":"","content":"Bullets ignore defense because they're too fast to see. If you can see them (with Quicken Sight), then you can generally use defense against them.<br /> <br /> Chucking a car is not too fast to see. You have from when they start moving to throw to get out of the way. There's plenty of time to hop three feet to the right to avoid the thing, or dive under it, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Chucking a car already gets the benefit of upgraded damage. It doesn't really need to ignore defense, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T13:13:16-07:00","id":1097855,"title":"","content":"I can kinda see what you're getting at here. Applying Defense to an attack is passive, it doesn't require an action to do so, and so you're left free to take a full action after shifting slightly to the left in order to avoid a punch. However, litterally throwing yourself to the side in order to avoid a minivan that comes flying your way does leave a lot of time for other actions.<br /> <br /> If you choose to represent this difference in your game, I think the idea you had was pretty solid. In order to get to use your Defense, you have to spend your action to dodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The 'e' is omitted on purpose and for stylistc reasons... I promise.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13322-aneas","name":"Aneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13322_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T22:14:09-07:00","id":1097985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aneas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097066-launching-big-object?p=1097855#post1097855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can kinda see what you're getting at here. Applying Defense to an attack is passive, it doesn't require an action to do so, and so you're left free to take a full action after shifting slightly to the left in order to avoid a punch. However, litterally throwing yourself to the side in order to avoid a minivan that comes flying your way does leave a lot of time for other actions.<br /> <br /> If you choose to represent this difference in your game, I think the idea you had was pretty solid. In order to get to use your Defense, you have to spend your action to dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes that's exactly what I meant <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> It's not enough to just move your body like a boxer to avoid a rolling car more than 4 meters large, in my opinion. In Exalted, for example, such kind of BIG attacks are simply considered unavoidable without stunt or charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T03:44:41-07:00","id":1098051,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, use the rules for Covering Fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T05:42:28-07:00","id":1098078,"title":"","content":"Rules say you actually aren't supposed to be able to Dodge when you can't apply Defense.<br /> <br /> Breaking this down, a car is around size 10 requiring an equal Strength + Vigor to throw with a weapon bonus of 3 or, for an additional Vitae cost, 3 + Vigor as a weapon bonus. As an improvised weapon the attack penalty is minor. With an expected 8 or more lethal damage for an attack, I think normal people would Dodge if they can. An Elder could potentially throw an SUV and it would be lethal damage even to vampires.<br /> <br /> Rather than eliminate Defense and fall into a problem when something with super Defense comes along that should be able to get up after being hit with a car because &quot;scary&quot;, if the intention is to &quot;encourage&quot; Dodging then it seems to me to be just as effective as anything to say the weapon bonus is Size + Durability. That would be Dodge or risk taking 13-18 damage at a minimum. If someone thinks they can shrug that off then let them try, I say.<br /> <br /> Allowing for the scene &quot;I hit you with a <i>fucking</i> car. How are you still standing?&quot; has its uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":".  mind was somewhere else 05-29-2017, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T09:40:07-07:00","id":1098122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097066-launching-big-object?p=1098078#post1098078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rather than eliminate Defense and fall into a problem when something with super Defense comes along that should be able to get up after being hit with a car because &quot;scary&quot;, if the intention is to &quot;encourage&quot; Dodging then it seems to me to be just as effective as anything to say the weapon bonus is Size + Durability. That would be Dodge or risk taking 13-18 damage at a minimum. If someone thinks they can shrug that off then let them try, I say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the intention is to &quot;encourage dodging&quot; but rather to just simulate that an action is required in order to avoid something that big. I'm not Marcus though, so I don't know what his/her intentions are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The 'e' is omitted on purpose and for stylistc reasons... I promise.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13322-aneas","name":"Aneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13322_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T13:07:57-07:00","id":1098203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aneas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1097066-launching-big-object?p=1098122#post1098122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the intention is to &amp;quot;encourage dodging&amp;quot; but rather to just simulate that an action is required in order to avoid something that big. I'm not Marcus though, so I don't know what his/her intentions are.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, this is exactly my point ov view, and you expressed it better than me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T13:36:33-07:00","id":1098214,"title":"","content":"Perhaps then there is a misunderstanding of the system. To avoid an attack an action is required because the only way to do that is to Dodge. A character can Defend to avoid damage from an attack but they would still get hit unless it was some &quot;Five Finger Death Punch&quot; situation. For example, a target might Defend to reduce the pool so that no successes are rolled; the car falls short and slides into the target pushing them back a few inches when the target puts their hands up to defend resulting in no damage.<br /> <br /> Or we can have something realistic. A person can &quot;roll with a punch&quot; and suffer no damage even if punched in the face bare-handed. I know as I have been sucker-punched before. I didn't even end up with a bruise. It was nothing more than a momentary sharp pain followed by a few minutes of dull pain. I successfully defended myself but I certainly was hit square in the jaw.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing how it is all or nothing with a car throw. The car doesn't have to fall on top of a character as in the Wicked Witch of the West. A car can &quot;clip&quot; a character as it flies by or slide into a character or any other thing someone can think of that would possible hurt.<br /> <br /> The system is very abstract mechanically. A successful Dodge means the attack was avoided. A failed attack roll means the attack was avoided or didn't have enough power to damage the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}